### ============================================================================
### 00 - Authentication & session bootstrap
### ============================================================================
### Every other file in http/ needs a valid PHPSESSID. Run this file first.
###
###   bWAPP password storage:  hash("sha1", $password)  -> login.php:36
###   static credentials:      bee / bug                -> admin/settings.php
###   (those same credentials are served unauthenticated on /admin/ - see 08-info-disclosure.http)
### ============================================================================

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Baseline - confirm the target is alive
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/login.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Accept: text/html
### Expected: 200 and a login form


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. LOGIN - grab the PHPSESSID from the Set-Cookie response header
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### The submit button is named `form`, NOT `login_submit`, and the security
### level is submitted in the same POST. Getting this wrong silently returns
### the login page again with a 200, which is a common false-negative.
###
### Copy the PHPSESSID value into http-client.env as @session.
POST {{baseUrl}}/login.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

login=bee&password=bug&security_level=0&form=submit
### Expected: 302 -> index.php, Set-Cookie: PHPSESSID=...


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. AUTHENTICATED BASELINE - prove the session works
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/portal.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
Accept: text/html
### Expected: 200, page shows "Welcome Bee" and the bug list


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Read the current user's secret (no authorization check at all)
###    BWAPP-AUTH-06 / A1 Broken Access Control
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/secret.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 200 text/plain -> "Your secret: <the secret>"


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Set the security level via the app's own endpoint
###    Proves the "protection" is nothing but a cookie the client controls.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/security_level_set.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

security_level=0&form=submit
### Expected: 302, Set-Cookie: security_level=0


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Logout
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/logout.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 302 -> login.php
